.TH "easel index" 1 "@EASEL_DATE@" "Easel @EASEL_VERSION@" "Easel Manual"

.SH NAME

easel index \- create SSI fast lookup index for sequences in sequence file


.SH SYNOPSIS

.B easel index
[\fIoptions\fR]
.I seqfile

.SH DESCRIPTION

.B easel index
creates a fast lookup index for the individual sequence names
and accessions in
.IR seqfile ,
and writes it to a file called
.IR seqfile .ssi.
.B easel sfetch
uses this index file to accelerate
retrieval of sequences or subsequences from 
.I seqfile.

.PP
Each sequence in
.I seqfile
must have a unique name, and optionally a unique accession (with the
.B \-a
option for indexing accessions too).



.SH OPTIONS

.TP
.B \-a
Index accessions (if present), in addition to sequence names/identifiers.

.TP
.B \-h
Print brief help; includes version number and summary of
all options.

.TP
.B \-u
Parse UniProt identifiers of the form "<db>|<acc>|<id>". Use <id>
as the sequence name; use <acc> as the sequence accession.
For example, given a sequence name of "sp|Q7V2C5|CSS4B_PROMP",
parse that into name "CSS4B_PROMP" and accession "Q7V2C5".

.TP
.BI \-\-informat " <fmt>"
Specify that input
.I <msafile>
is in format
.IR <fmt> ,
and bypass format autodetection.
Choices for
.I <fmt>
are:
.BR stockholm|pfam|a2m|afa|psiblast|clustal|clustallike|phylip|phylips|selex .
